{
  "name": "Archive and log invoices from Gmail with SFTP and Google Sheets — V2",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nFor small teams that archive supplier invoices and maintain an invoice register. Run manually or every six hours: Gmail retrieves matching messages, each PDF becomes one item, and text extraction feeds a configurable parser. Four example provider categories route validated invoices to SFTP, then insert or update one Google Sheets row using `Provider:Invoice Number` as the Unique Key. Source emails are retained.\n\nText-based PDFs only; OCR and AI are not included. Unknown providers, missing fields and invalid dates or amounts stop processing. Repeated runs upload the same filename again; Sheets upserts do not prevent SFTP overwrites.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Gmail OAuth2 in the Gmail node; narrow its query to your invoice senders and review the 30-day lookback.\n2. In **Parse invoice and canonical name**, adapt provider patterns, field regexes and destination paths to your PDFs. Dates accept ISO or day/month/year; amounts accept decimal and grouped European/US formats.\n3. Connect all four SFTP nodes. Create writable `/invoices/utilities`, `/invoices/internet`, `/invoices/cloud` and `/invoices/hosting` folders, or change the parser paths.\n4. Create an `Invoices` worksheet with headers: `Provider`, `Category`, `Invoice Number`, `Date`, `Amount`, `File`, `Unique Key`. Replace `REPLACE_WITH_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID` in all four Sheets nodes, connect a Google service account and share the spreadsheet with it as Editor.\n5. Test each provider and a multi-PDF email; compare files and rows, then rerun an invoice before enabling the schedule.\n\n### Customization\nAdjust the schedule, Gmail query, provider rules and column mappings. Keep provider names aligned with the four routing filters.",
        "height": 1016,
        "width": 636,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "cf62e776-c0a6-40f4-9db8-3565cf02e0ab",
      "name": "00 — WORKFLOW OVERVIEW",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -800,
        -256
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 01 · Start a controlled run\nUse Manual Trigger for setup checks. The schedule repeats every six hours once the workflow is published; leave it inactive until all credentials, folders and parsing rules are configured.",
        "height": 578,
        "width": 362,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "7ec9cb04-5c5e-446e-ad9d-1f55ecf6fbb4",
      "name": "01 — TRIGGERS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -160,
        -48
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 02 · Collect individual invoice PDFs\nSearch matching mail from the last 30 days and download attachments. Keep PDFs as separate linked items, skip other attachments and reject PDFs larger than 20 MiB.",
        "height": 578,
        "width": 904,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "217c4d62-d7f8-4635-b9dc-4fa6e4f38cb4",
      "name": "02 — GMAIL INTAKE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        240,
        -48
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 03 · Turn PDF text into invoice records\nCustomize the four provider patterns and field regexes in the parser. Unsupported, ambiguous or incomplete invoices stop execution before upload; scanned PDFs need an OCR step.",
        "height": 578,
        "width": 638,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "56f236bd-5ca3-4b34-8e84-772ff9a6c3f4",
      "name": "03 — EXTRACT & VALIDATE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1168,
        -48
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 04 · Archive first, then update the register\nEach category uploads its PDF, restores the matching invoice and upserts the same Invoices worksheet. SFTP/Sheets retry up to three attempts; repeat uploads may overwrite files. Emails stay in Gmail; failures stop without a notification branch.",
        "height": 1088,
        "width": 1266,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "ad889340-5715-4c15-a175-81ba92f2d607",
      "name": "04 — STORAGE & COMPLETION",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1824,
        -256
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "5e6ef999-f2a0-4a79-bfb4-3d195591fc61",
      "name": "Manual Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        -48,
        160
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
